issue.description:
Add a new top-level preview tab named "App shells" that shows how the current Personal UI theme feels when applied to different application-shell/sidebar patterns.

Intent:
Give users a live visual reference for app-level chrome and navigation structure without turning the preview into a full application mockup.

Target preview tab order:

1. Cards
2. Design system
3. App shells
4. States

Core principle:

* App shells is a live preview surface, not an editor.
* Theme/sidebar controls remain in the existing Workbench sidebar.
* The shell previews should update immediately when the active theme or sidebar tokens change.
* Focus on shell/chrome structure, especially sidebar design, rather than detailed application content.

1. Shell showcase scope

Create several distinct app-shell/sidebar examples using the accepted shadcn Sidebar system and current Personal UI tokens.

Possible shell directions include:

* classic full-height sidebar;
* inset/floating sidebar;
* icon-collapsible sidebar;
* compact utility sidebar;
* grouped/navigation-heavy sidebar;
* sidebar plus secondary header/breadcrumb treatment.

These are directions, not a required checklist. The worker may curate a smaller set of strong shell variations.

Each shell should demonstrate meaningful differences in:

* sidebar width/proportion;
* grouping/navigation density;
* active-item treatment;
* header/chrome relationship;
* border/surface treatment;
* sidebar/background contrast;
* spacing/radius;
* typography hierarchy;
* collapsed/expanded behavior where appropriate.

2. Main content treatment

The right/main content area of each shell should remain intentionally abstract.

Use simple neutral silhouette/skeleton shapes to suggest application content, such as:

* blank card rectangles;
* muted content blocks;
* simple header bars;
* placeholder rows/sections.

Do not build full dashboards, forms, tables, charts, or real app workflows inside these shell previews.

The goal is to keep attention on the app shell itself.

3. Theme/token linkage

App shell previews must use the same live theme state as the rest of the Workbench.

Changes from the sidebar should reflect immediately, including:

* semantic colors;
* typography;
* spacing/radius;
* border/shadow behavior where relevant;
* light/dark mode;
* sidebar-token activation and dedicated sidebar values.

When dedicated sidebar tokens are OFF, shells should reflect the accepted sidebar fallback/alias behavior.
When dedicated sidebar tokens are ON, shells should reflect the dedicated sidebar token set.

4. shadcn-first implementation

* Use the existing official shadcn Sidebar architecture/components already accepted in Personal UI.
* Do not invent a parallel custom sidebar framework for this tab.
* Use existing layout primitives and semantic tokens.
* Custom composition/layout code is acceptable for arranging multiple shell examples, but sidebar behavior should stay aligned with the accepted shadcn Sidebar system.

5. Interaction

Keep interaction lightweight and useful:

* shell examples may support sidebar collapse/expand if that is part of the demonstrated pattern;
* active navigation state may be selectable;
* hover/focus states should work;
* no workflow-heavy app behavior is needed.

Interaction must not materially destabilize overall preview geometry.

6. Visual quality

Design direction:

* clean and polished;
* simple but believable app chrome;
* restrained content silhouettes;
* clear variation between shell styles;
* portfolio-quality presentation;
* avoid noisy placeholder content.

Do not:

* duplicate editing controls inside App shells;
* create a second theme state;
* hard-code raw colors where semantic tokens exist;
* build full app screens inside each shell;
* add unrelated public resources solely for this preview;
* change Theme v3, history, persistence, Design Command, or token semantics.

Accessibility / responsiveness:

* preserve top-level Tabs keyboard/focus semantics;
* sidebar examples should preserve appropriate keyboard/focus behavior for demonstrated controls;
* previews should reflow without page-level horizontal overflow;
* shell cards/examples may stack at narrower widths;
* maintain logical reading order.

Acceptance:

* A new top-level "App shells" tab appears between Design system and States.
* Cards, Design system, and States continue to function unchanged.
* App shells contains multiple distinct sidebar/app-shell previews.
* Shells use the accepted shadcn Sidebar system rather than a custom replacement.
* Main content areas use simple silhouette/skeleton placeholders rather than full application UIs.
* Theme edits update the shell previews live.
* Dedicated sidebar-token ON/OFF behavior is reflected correctly.
* Light/dark rendering is coherent.
* No duplicate theme controls/state are introduced.
* No unnecessary public resource expansion is introduced.
* Existing tab, sidebar, accessibility, persistence, history, and Design Command behavior remain intact.
